      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Farrell set to recall Gibson-Park as Sheehan misses Fiji test with concussion",
          "body": "Ireland head coach Andy Farrell is set to restore scrum-half Jamison Gibson-Park to the starting XV for Saturday's Nations Championship match, with hooker Rónan Kelleher expected to start after captain Dan Sheehan was ruled out of the Fiji fixture with concussion. The expectation is that Farrell avoids sweeping changes, so Fiji, ranked ninth in the world and coached by Jake White, face a largely settled Ireland side. Gibson-Park came off the bench against Argentina, with Craig Casey starting at nine in that win."
        },
