    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-12",
      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad unrest",
          "heading": "Jamie George questions Times report of senior players' demands for Borthwick talks",
          "body": "A Times report claiming senior players had demanded talks with England head coach Steve Borthwick and senior RFU figures dominated the build-up to Sunday's 45-22 win over Australia, England's most points against the Wallabies. Vice-captain Jamie George questioned both its contents and its timing. World Cup winner Ben Kay calls a fully harmonious changing room naïve and says that in situations like this, \"it can actually galvanise the players and bring them together a little bit more.\" Kay adds that winning makes players forget earlier grumbles."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan ruled out of Fiji game with concussion",
          "body": "France captain Antoine Dupont starts at fly-half against Springboks."
