        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Farrell expected to restore Gibson-Park to Ireland's starting XV against Fiji",
          "body": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan is out of Saturday's Fiji game with concussion, the42 reports, and Rónan Kelleher is expected to start at hooker in his place. Ireland scrum-half Jamison Gibson-Park, who came off the bench against Argentina while Craig Casey started at nine, looks likely to return to the starting XV alongside Sam Prendergast. James Ryan is also in contention for the second row, and Ireland head coach Andy Farrell may avoid sweeping changes against a Fiji side ranked ninth in the world."
        },
