      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Defensive review",
          "heading": "Len Ikitau says Wallabies must connect forwards and backline better against Scotland",
          "body": "Australia have conceded 138 points across their three-game losing run, an average of 46 a game, and defence is the first thing to fix before Scotland. Ikitau described the problem as one of connection: \"We need to be able to connect well with our forwards and then with our backfield too.\" Ikitau has had a different midfield partner in three straight matches and will likely reunite with Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii, with Kurtley Beale and Filipo Daugunu the other options."
        },
