      "edition": "Thursday 12 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical admission",
          "heading": "Eddie Jones concedes Japan must break up the game to beat England",
          "body": "Japan head coach Eddie Jones has laid out his route to an upset at Twickenham on Saturday. “We’ll need to be able to break up the game, if we play an orthodox game of rugby, we’re probably going to struggle to beat them,” the Australian said, ahead of a match Japan are expected to enter as overwhelming underdogs. Japan have lost all six previous Test meetings with England, most recently 54-19 on their autumn visit two years ago."
        },
        {
